{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"handwoven-unthankful-reindeer","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Follow-up from d19d LLM-Review (Gerrit change 1776, advisory comments — d19d landed with LLM-Review +1).\n\nFour advisory findings to harden the many-to-many outbound path:\n\n1. (correctness) Case-sensitivity mismatch: the create-path membership check in outbound_differ._compute_outbound_create_mutation uses `target not in mapping.projects` (case-SENSITIVE), while the applier's cross-project guard normalizes both sides to uppercase. A bridge_project differing in case from the mapping key (e.g. 'b' vs 'B') would suppress the create but pass the guard. Jira project keys are canonically uppercase and the mapping is seeded from them, so this does not trigger in practice, but the two paths should agree. Make the create-path check case-insensitive (or normalize both consistently).\n\n2. (tests) The applier's new many-to-many guard branch (list(read_projects(repo_root).keys()) or _project fed to _cross_project_targets) is only unit-tested at the pure helper level with a literal set; the store-loading wiring in the caller is not exercised end-to-end. Add an integration test that seeds projects.json and drives the guard through the caller.\n\n3. (tests) run_differs newly threads load_mapping(repo_root) into the outbound diff; the comment asserts a malformed projects.json fails closed (ValueError aborts the pass) but there is no test at the run_differs seam proving it. Add one.\n\n4. (correctness) The projects mapping is read twice from disk per pass — load_mapping in run_differs (create resolution) and read_projects in applier (guard set). A mid-pass projects.json change could make them disagree. Consider threading one read through, or accept + document (single-pass window; projects.json changes are rare CLI writes). Low priority.\n\nNone are regressions; the create-path resolution is new behavior gated on a seeded mapping (not live until a store seeds projects.json).","id":"7b9a-f855-b2e4-49f9","parent_id":"0e68-41eb-5782-4336","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"M2M outbound: case-insensitive project membership + guard-wiring test depth"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786720928170448001,"uuid":"4d61c73f-9cef-4c75-abc7-5d690150b5ac"}